          <caption>
            <p>Pattern of X-Linked Inheritance. Daughters inherit one X chromosome from each parent, whereas sons inherit the X chromosome from the mother and the Y chromosome from the father, resulting in characteristic transmission patterns of X-linked traits. Contributed by DK Yadav, MBBS</p>
